From 3ce38fcf419a6159bed61ad83371e89ab686d3bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:00:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][PlayerInfo] Processed in every frame while a control
 of the panel animates

The player information is processed at most four times a second while
nothing is asked of it and nothing of it moves, so that the GUI pass
of most frames can be left out. Kodi runs the animation of a control
only in the frames that process it: the animations of a skin's own
panel (a row that fades in or out with its visibility, a focus, a
conditional animation) would have run at four frames a second.

The panel is now processed in every frame while a control of it
animates (any type of animation but none), and at once where a
condition of a control has changed since it was last processed (its
visibility, the condition of a conditional animation), so that the
animation starts in the same frame as before (CPlayerInfoRefresh::
Animates(), CGUIControl::ConditionsChanged(), CAnimation::
ConditionChanged(), which look and change nothing). Only the controls
that a processed frame would process are looked at: those of the groups
that are shown. While nothing animates the panel is processed four
times a second, as before. Estuary's panel and Hades' own have no such
animation; for them the only change is that a row that shows or hides
does so in the frame its condition changes, not up to 250 ms later.
